3. Prohibited without prior written permission of the copyright holder:
   a) copying, reproducing or downloading the Source Code for use (other than
      automatic caching while viewing);
   b) modifying the Source Code or creating derivative works;
   c) using the Source Code or any part of it in any other software, product or
      service, commercial or not;
   d) building, compiling, running or distributing builds made from the Source
      Code, modified or not;
   e) distributing, publishing, sublicensing, selling, renting or otherwise
      transferring the Source Code to third parties;
   f) using the Source Code to train, fine-tune or evaluate machine-learning
      models or to create datasets;
   g) removing or altering copyright notices or this license.

4. Official builds. Official OpsOpsAi builds published by the copyright holder
   are provided free of charge under the terms published with them. This
   license grants no rights to the Source Code beyond section 2.

5. GitHub forks. The ability to fork through GitHub, where GitHub's terms
   provide it, grants no rights beyond section 2: a fork may only be viewed.

6. Contributions. By submitting changes (pull request, patch, issue with code)
   you grant the copyright holder a free, perpetual, non-exclusive right to use,
